@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@schoolId = 918a27f3-2321-4f69-a15c-9c61f9f4f818
@termId = 43530ca6-bd8f-4cf1-b45e-288ce29750d0
@windowId = c2ffbc99-9c0b-4ef8-bb6d-6bb9bd380c33

### Note: With cookie-based authentication, ensure your HTTP client (like VS Code REST Client) 
### automatically manages and sends cookies received from login responses (e.g., via a cookie jar).

### 1. Create a new academic term (Admin / School Admin)
POST {{baseUrl}}/terms
Content-Type: application/json
# Authorization header removed; authentication handled automatically via HTTP cookies

{
  "schoolId": "{{schoolId}}",
  "academicYear": "2026",
  "termName": "Term 1",
  "startDate": "2026-01-05",
  "endDate": "2026-04-10",
  "status": "active",
  "isCurrentTerm": true
}

### 2. List all academic terms for a school (Any Authenticated User: Admin, Teacher, Student, Parent)
GET {{baseUrl}}/terms/school/{{schoolId}}
# Authorization header removed; authentication handled automatically via HTTP cookies

### 3. Get the current active academic term for a school (Any Authenticated User)
GET {{baseUrl}}/terms/school/{{schoolId}}/current
# Authorization header removed; authentication handled automatically via HTTP cookies

### 4. Get a specific academic term by ID (Any Authenticated User)
GET {{baseUrl}}/terms/{{termId}}
# Authorization header removed; authentication handled automatically via HTTP cookies

### 5. Update an academic term (Admin / School Admin)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/terms/{{termId}}
Content-Type: application/json
# Authorization header removed; authentication handled automatically via HTTP cookies

{
  "termName": "Term 1 (Revised)",
  "status": "active"
}

### 6. Create a term window/sub-period e.g. Mid-Term Break (Admin / School Admin)
POST {{baseUrl}}/terms/windows
Content-Type: application/json
# Authorization header removed; authentication handled automatically via HTTP cookies

{
  "termId": "{{termId}}",
  "windowType": "mid_term_break",
  "title": "Term 1 Mid-Term Break",
  "startDate": "2026-02-20",
  "endDate": "2026-02-24"
}

### 7. List all windows for an academic term (Any Authenticated User)
GET {{baseUrl}}/terms/{{termId}}/windows
# Authorization header removed; authentication handled automatically via HTTP cookies

### 8. Delete a term window (Admin / School Admin)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/terms/windows/{{windowId}}
# Authorization header removed; authentication handled automatically via HTTP cookies

### 9. Delete an academic term (Super Admin only)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/terms/{{termId}}
# Authorization header removed; authentication handled automatically via HTTP cookies